[b]Adaptive Arithmetic Candles[/b]

[b]What it does[/b]
Replaces raw price bars with an efficiency-adaptive candle transform and colors each candle by its direction and whether the regression slope agrees, so a move that carries through stands apart from a counter-slope candle.

[b]Adaptive Candles[/b]
[list]
[*]Kaufman-efficiency-adaptive smoothing of a weighted close/typical/regression blend — reacts fast in efficient moves, damps in choppy ones
[*]Regression-anchored close with a trend-pressure body boost (slope + body strength)
[*]Synthetic wicks scaled from real wick proportions, widened when the market is noisy
[*]Strong vs. weak bull/bear coloring: strong when candle direction and regression slope agree
[/list]

[b]Flip Signals (early warning)[/b]
[list]
[*]Bullish/Bearish flip markers fire when the candle direction changes and the regression slope points the same way
[*]A flip alone is not a trade signal — it just marks a state change
[/list]

[b]Long/Short Signals (the actual trigger)[/b]
[list]
[*]Fire on a strong bull/bear state confirmed by a close breaking the prior N bars' high/low
[*]Only the first break of each strong run fires
[*]Structure break, not candle color, is what triggers the signal
[*]Built-in alerts for flips and for Long/Short signals
[/list]

